:: StoryTitle
The Quiet Floor

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "9C70DA1C-07D2-4F9A-9168-7D77E88D6301",
  "format": "SugarCube",
  "format-version": "2.37.3",
  "start": "Start"
}

:: StoryInit
<<set $inventory = []>>
<<set $clues = []>>
<<set $bellRings = false>>
<<set $foundNote = false>>
<<set $sawPortrait = false>>
<<set $sawClock = false>>
<<set $sawCrate = false>>
<<set $deskOpen = false>>
<<set $elevatorUnlocked = false>>
<<set $deskCodeInput = "">>

:: UIWidgets [widget]
<<widget "addItem">>
<<if !$inventory.includes(_args[0])>>
  <<run $inventory.push(_args[0])>>
<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "addClue">>
<<if !$clues.includes(_args[0])>>
  <<run $clues.push(_args[0])>>
<</if>>
<</widget>>

:: StoryCaption
[[🏠 Main Menu->Start]]

''🎒 Inventory:''
<<if $inventory.length is 0>>
- Empty
<<else>>
<<for _item range $inventory>>
- <<= _item>>
<</for>>
<</if>>

''🧩 Clues:''
<<if $clues.length is 0>>
- None yet
<<else>>
<<for _clue range $clues>>
- <<= _clue>>
<</for>>
<</if>>

:: StoryStyles [stylesheet]
.room-map {
  border: 1px solid #3a3a3a;
  padding: 0.75rem;
  margin-top: 0.75rem;
  background: #121212;
}

.room-map table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
}

.room-map td {
  text-align: center;
  padding: 0.45rem;
  border: 1px dashed #2a2a2a;
}

.room-map .blank {
  border-color: transparent;
}

:: Start
The house has a slate board in the front hall.

Choose a door:
- [[🚪 Door 1: The Quiet Floor->Quiet Floor]]
- [[🚪 Door 2: Locked for now 🔒->Door 2 Locked]]
- [[🚪 Door 3: Locked for now 🔒->Door 3 Locked]]

:: Door 2 Locked
Door 2 does not move when you pull the handle.

A brass tag reads: "Under construction."

[[Back to door list->Start]]

:: Door 3 Locked
Door 3 is sealed with painted-over screws.

Someone penciled beside it: "Come back later."

[[Back to door list->Start]]

:: Quiet Floor
The bell has not rung yet, but you can feel it in the walls.

You wake in a small guest room with no windows, only a brass plaque:

''GUEST ROOM - QUIET FLOOR''

A folded note is pinned to the door with a silver nail.

<<if !$foundNote>>
[[📝 Read the note->Read Note]]
<</if>>
[[🚶 Step into the foyer->Foyer]]

:: Read Note
The paper smells faintly of smoke and rain.

"If you are reading this, the house accepted you.
Find Ada before the Bell.
Do not trust the mirrors.
- E"

<<set $foundNote = true>>
<<addClue "A note signed only 'E'.">>

[[🚶 Go to the foyer->Foyer]]

:: Foyer
A circular foyer sits at the center of this floor.

You orient yourself by direction instead of door labels.

<div class="room-map">
<table>
  <tr>
    <td class="blank"></td>
    <td>[[🌿 Conservatory->Conservatory]]</td>
    <td class="blank"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>[[📚 Study->Study]]</td>
    <td><strong>Foyer</strong></td>
    <td>[[🔧 Service Hall->Service Hall]]</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="blank"></td>
    <td>[[🛏️ Guest Room->Quiet Floor]]</td>
    <td class="blank"></td>
  </tr>
</table>
</div>

A tall portrait watches from above the stairs.

[[🖼️ Inspect Portrait->Portrait]]

:: Portrait
The brass plate under the portrait reads:

"''SEVEN'' guests entered Aster House in 1924.
Only one left with a name."

<<if !$sawPortrait>>
<<set $sawPortrait = true>>
<<addClue "Portrait plate emphasizes SEVEN.">>
<</if>>

[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]

:: Study
Dust hangs in sheets. A roll-top desk sits against the wall.

<<if $deskOpen>>
The desk stands open. A hidden compartment is empty.
[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]
<<else>>
A keypad has been added to the antique lock. Three digits.

<<if $sawPortrait and $sawClock and $sawCrate>>
You have enough fragments to test a full code.

The house gave you three signs: the frozen time, the watcher above, and the freight mark.
<</if>>

Code: <<textbox "$deskCodeInput" "" autofocus>>

<<button "Try code 🔢">>
  <<if $deskCodeInput is "873">>
    <<set $deskOpen = true>>
    <<addItem "Brass Service Key">>
    <<addClue "Desk letter: 'The Bell is not a clock. It is a person.'">>
    <<goto "Desk Open">>
  <<else>>
    <<goto "Desk Fail">>
  <</if>>
<</button>>

[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]
<</if>>

:: Desk Fail
The lock flashes red once, then goes dark.

The house hums, as if amused.

[[Try again->Study]]
[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]

:: Desk Open
The lock clicks.

Inside:
- A brass key tagged "SERVICE ELEVATOR"
- A torn letter in Ada's handwriting

"The Bell keeps the floor plans in people, not paper.
If I disappear, follow the freight line down."

[[🗝️ Take everything and return to the foyer->Foyer]]

:: Conservatory
The glass ceiling is cracked but dry. Dead vines coil around iron benches.

At the center, a frozen station clock still reads ''8:17''.

<<if !$sawClock>>
<<set $sawClock = true>>
<<addClue "Conservatory clock stopped at 8:17.">>
<</if>>

You hear faint knocking from inside a sealed wall.

[[🧱 Examine the sealed wall->Sealed Wall]]
[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]

:: Sealed Wall
You press your ear to the plaster.

Three knocks. Pause. Three knocks.

Not random. A signal.

<<addClue "Knock pattern: 3 - pause - 3.">>

[[Back to the conservatory->Conservatory]]

:: Service Hall
Pipes run along the ceiling. At the end of the hall waits a caged service elevator.

A wooden freight crate sits nearby, stenciled with a faded number: ''3''.

<<if !$sawCrate>>
<<set $sawCrate = true>>
<<addClue "Freight crate marked 3.">>
<</if>>

<<if $elevatorUnlocked>>
The elevator gate is open.
[[⬇️ Descend to the freight level->Freight Level]]
[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]
<<else>>
<<if $inventory.includes("Brass Service Key")>>
You fit the brass key into the elevator lock.

<<button "Unlock the service elevator 🔓">>
  <<set $elevatorUnlocked = true>>
  <<goto "Elevator Unlock">>
<</button>>
<<else>>
The elevator lock has no keypad. It needs a key.
<</if>>

[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]
<</if>>

:: Elevator Unlock
The gate rattles open.

A fresh card has been tied to the control lever:

"FREIGHT LEVEL - OCCUPANT: ADA MARROW"

The ink is still wet.

[[⬇️ Descend->Freight Level]]
[[Back to the foyer->Foyer]]

:: Freight Level
The elevator drops too far.

When it stops, you step into a corridor of unfinished walls and numbered doors.
The guest room mark is here too.

At the far end, a woman in a bellhop coat waits under a bare light.
She smiles like she has been expecting you.

"You took your time," she says.
"Now tell me: which name did the house give you?"

''End of Chapter 1 starter.''

[[🔄 Restart->Start Over]]

:: Start Over
<<set $inventory = []>>
<<set $clues = []>>
<<set $bellRings = false>>
<<set $foundNote = false>>
<<set $sawPortrait = false>>
<<set $sawClock = false>>
<<set $sawCrate = false>>
<<set $deskOpen = false>>
<<set $elevatorUnlocked = false>>
